# testdata.consts
#
# Shared constants for the scripts/testdata-create/ pipeline.
#
# This file is:
#  - `source`d directly by the bash scripts in this folder (e.g. `3_run_sarek_vc`), and
#  - parsed by the Python scripts via `consts_loader.py` (which sources it in a real
#    shell subprocess to resolve the `$(...)` command substitutions below).
#
# Keep this file restricted to plain `KEY="value"` lines (bash-sourceable as-is, and
# simple enough for consts_loader.py to parse). Only `$(cd ... && pwd)`-style command
# substitution is used, to derive absolute paths relative to this file's own location.
#
# The dataset described here (fixed 10-sample 1000 Genomes exome cohort, 2 trios) is
# intentionally fixed and not meant to be parametrized further - see AGENTS.md and
# artifacts/1_plan.md. Do not add CLI flags or extra parametrization to the scripts that
# read this file; edit this file directly if the fixed dataset ever needs to change.

DATASET_NAME="control_set_small_v2"

# Single hardcoded work directory; all other paths below are derived from it.
WORKDIR="$(cd "$(dirname "${BASH_SOURCE[0]:-$0}")" && pwd)/workdir"

CRAMS_DIR="$WORKDIR/crams"
SAREK_SAMPLESHEET="$WORKDIR/$DATASET_NAME.sarek-samplesheet.csv"
SAREK_WORKDIR="$WORKDIR/sarek.workdir"
SAREK_OUTDIR="$WORKDIR/sarek.outdir"
JOINT_GERMLINE_VCF="$SAREK_OUTDIR/variant_calling/haplotypecaller/joint_variant_calling/joint_germline.vcf.gz"
VCF_PREQC_DIR="$WORKDIR/vcfs_pre-qc"
METADATA_DIR="$WORKDIR/metadata"

# VEP annotation via wtsi-hgi/nf_vep_annotation (scripts/testdata-create/7_run_vep_annotation).
# VEP_ANNOTATION_REVISION is the one place to bump once split_test is merged to main.
VEP_ANNOTATION_REVISION="split_test"

VEP_DATA_DIR="$WORKDIR/vep_data"
VEP_ANNOTATION_WORKDIR="$WORKDIR/vep_annotation.workdir"
VEP_ANNOTATION_RESULTS_DIR="$WORKDIR/vep_annotation_results"


# Reused static resources (read-only), shared with artifacts/public-dataset-build/.
IGSR_SAMPLES_TSV="igsr_samples.tsv"
EXOME_TARGETS_BED="hg38_exome_v2.0.2_targets_sorted_validated.re_annotated.padded50.bed"

# Fixed sample set: 10 samples, "SAMPLE_ID:POPULATION:SEX" tokens, space-separated.
# Includes trio CEU1 (NA12878/NA12891/NA12892) and trio YRI1 (NA19240/NA19239/NA19238),
# plus 4 unrelated samples spanning other populations.
SAMPLES="NA12878:CEU:female NA12891:CEU:male NA12892:CEU:female NA19238:YRI:female NA19239:YRI:male NA19240:YRI:female HG00584:CHS:female NA19798:MXL:male NA20778:TSI:male NA20903:GIH:male"

# Fixed trio definitions: "FAMILY_ID:CHILD:FATHER:MOTHER" tokens, space-separated.
TRIOS="CEU1:NA12878:NA12891:NA12892 YRI1:NA19240:NA19239:NA19238"

# GIAB AshkenazimTrio + ChineseTrio addition (scripts/testdata-create/1a_download_giab_trios).
#
# Kept as separate constants rather than merged into SAMPLES/TRIOS, since GIAB_SAMPLES tokens
# carry a 4th field (BAM_URL) that SAMPLES tokens don't, and 1_download_crams.py's formulaic
# 1000-Genomes URL construction doesn't apply to GIAB samples. Read both by the bash script
# 1a_download_giab_trios (which `source`s this file directly, like 3_run_sarek_vc does) and,
# via consts_loader.py's get_giab_samples()/get_giab_trios(), by 2_make_sarek_manifest.py,
# 4_make_sex_info.py, and 5_make_trios_fam.py, which merge them alongside SAMPLES/TRIOS.
#
# Each GIAB FTP sample has its own ad hoc directory/file naming (unlike 1000 Genomes' uniform
# layout), so the source URL is recorded per sample here rather than constructed by a formula.
# Kept on one physical line each (like SAMPLES/TRIOS) so consts_loader.py's line-based
# `_discover_keys()` (which validates every KEY="value" line's quoting, even for keys it
# doesn't otherwise use) still sees one balanced-quote assignment per key.
#
# All 6 samples only have real Illumina exome data aligned to GRCh37 (or no exome data at
# all for HG006/HG007) - see artifacts/4_plan_giab_trios.md - so these instead point at each
# sample's whole-genome GRCh38 BAM; 1a_download_giab_trios slices out just the padded exome
# target regions.
#
# GIAB_BAMS_DIR: destination for the sliced per-sample exome BAM/BAI produced by
# 1a_download_giab_trios.
GIAB_BAMS_DIR="$WORKDIR/giab_bams"

# GIAB_SAMPLES: "SAMPLE_ID:POPULATION:SEX:BAM_URL" tokens, space-separated. POPULATION is a
# documentation label (AJ = Ashkenazi Jewish, CHN = Han Chinese), not a real 1000G population
# code, and (unlike SAMPLES) is not used to construct the URL.
GIAB_SAMPLES="HG002:AJ:male:https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/ReferenceSamples/giab/data/AshkenazimTrio/HG002_NA24385_son/NIST_Illumina_2x250bps/novoalign_bams/HG002.GRCh38.2x250.bam HG003:AJ:male:https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/ReferenceSamples/giab/data/AshkenazimTrio/HG003_NA24149_father/NIST_Illumina_2x250bps/novoalign_bams/HG003.GRCh38.2x250.bam HG004:AJ:female:https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/ReferenceSamples/giab/data/AshkenazimTrio/HG004_NA24143_mother/NIST_Illumina_2x250bps/novoalign_bams/HG004.GRCh38.2x250.bam HG005:CHN:male:https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/ReferenceSamples/giab/data/ChineseTrio/HG005_NA24631_son/HG005_NA24631_son_HiSeq_300x/NHGRI_Illumina300X_Chinesetrio_novoalign_bams/HG005.GRCh38_full_plus_hs38d1_analysis_set_minus_alts.300x.bam HG006:CHN:male:https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/ReferenceSamples/giab/data/ChineseTrio/HG006_NA24694-huCA017E_father/NA24694_Father_HiSeq100x/NHGRI_Illumina100X_Chinesetrio_novoalign_bams/HG006.GRCh38_full_plus_hs38d1_analysis_set_minus_alts.100x.bam HG007:CHN:female:https://ftp.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/ReferenceSamples/giab/data/ChineseTrio/HG007_NA24695-hu38168_mother/NA24695_Mother_HiSeq100x/NHGRI_Illumina100X_Chinesetrio_novoalign_bams/HG007.GRCh38_full_plus_hs38d1_analysis_set_minus_alts.100x.bam"

# GIAB_TRIOS: "FAMILY_ID:CHILD:FATHER:MOTHER" tokens, space-separated - same shape as TRIOS.
# Not read by 1a_download_giab_trios itself (which only needs GIAB_SAMPLES); recorded here as
# the declarative definition of the fixed trio structure, for a later script to consume.
GIAB_TRIOS="AshkenazimTrio:HG002:HG003:HG004 ChineseTrio:HG005:HG006:HG007"
